    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάφων-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>discordant, inconsistent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱστορίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					4.55
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1039d
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>
			<i>with</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				16
			</span></i>; esp. in Music, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάφωνον
			ἕλκειν</span> strike a <i>false note,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Damox.
				2.61
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i> (metaph. of tastes), etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμφωνος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				<u>Sect.Can.Praef.</u>
			</span></i>, Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.49H.
			</span></i>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1137c
				</span></i>
			: c.dat., <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.170
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἵστασθαι πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.90S.
				</span></i>
			</div>
